# CODEOWNERS — enforces the two-layer governance model.
#
# The CORE RULES LAYER is owned by a limited set of maintainers. Any PR that
# touches these paths must be reviewed by a code owner. This is what keeps the
# central layer controlled.
#
# Replace the placeholder handles below with your real maintainer team, and
# enable "Require review from Code Owners" in branch protection.

# --- Core rules: movement, collision, scoring, the schema contract ---
/js/config.js   @gotham-core
/js/schema.js   @gotham-core
/js/engine.js   @gotham-core

# --- App shell & tooling ---
/js/main.js     @gotham-core
/js/editor.js   @gotham-core

# --- Docs that define the contract ---
/docs/          @gotham-core
/CODEOWNERS     @gotham-core

# --- The STREET LAYER is intentionally NOT owned here ---
# streets/** has no code owner, so community street PRs can be reviewed and
# merged by a broader group (with the validator as the safety gate).
